  Scenario: Successfully submit supporting documentation
    Given I am an applicant
    And I have completed my application form
    When I upload the required supporting documents
    And I click the submit button
    Then I should see a confirmation message
    And my documents should be marked as submitted

  Scenario: Fail to submit supporting documentation due to missing documents
    Given I am an applicant
    And I have completed my application form
    When I attempt to submit without uploading all required documents
    Then I should see an error message indicating missing documents
    And my documents should not be marked as submitted

  Scenario: Fail to submit supporting documentation due to invalid file format
    Given I am an applicant
    And I have completed my application form
    When I upload a document in an invalid file format
    And I click the submit button
    Then I should see an error message indicating invalid file format
    And my documents should not be marked as submitted
```

### (2) Step Definitions in Python

```python
from behave import given, when, then

@given('I am an applicant')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant = Applicant()

@given('I have completed my application form')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant.complete_application_form()

@when('I upload the required supporting documents')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant.upload_supporting_documents()

@when('I click the submit button')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant.click_submit_button()

@then('I should see a confirmation message')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.applicant.get_confirmation_message() == "Your documents have been submitted successfully."

@then('my documents should be marked as submitted')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.applicant.documents_status() == "submitted"

@when('I attempt to submit without uploading all required documents')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant.attempt_submit_without_all_documents()

@then('I should see an error message indicating missing documents')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.applicant.get_error_message() == "Please upload all required documents."

@then('my documents should not be marked as submitted')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.applicant.documents_status() != "submitted"

@when('I upload a document in an invalid file format')
def step_impl(context):
    context.applicant.upload_invalid_format_document()

@then('I should see an error message indicating invalid file format')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.applicant.get_error_message() == "Invalid file format. Please upload a valid document."
```

### (3) Validation Checklist

- [ ] Verify that the applicant can access the document submission page.
- [ ] Verify that the applicant can upload supporting documents.
- [ ] Verify that the submit button is enabled after uploading documents.
- [ ] Verify that a confirmation message is displayed upon successful submission.
- [ ] Verify that documents are marked as submitted after successful submission.
- [ ] Verify that an error message is displayed if the applicant attempts to submit without uploading all required documents.
- [ ] Verify that documents are not marked as submitted if submission fails due to missing documents.
- [ ] Verify that an error message is displayed if the applicant uploads a document in an invalid file format.
- [ ] Verify that documents are not marked as submitted if submission fails due to invalid file format.

