**(1) Gherkin Scenarios in .feature format:**

```gherkin
Feature: Private Data Packages

  Scenario: Create a private data package
    Given I am logged in as a Publisher
    When I create a new data package
    And I set the data package visibility to private
    Then the data package should be marked as private
    And only my team should have access to the data package

  Scenario: Share a private data package with team
    Given I have a private data package
    When I share the data package with my team
    Then my team should receive access to the data package
    And no one outside my team should have access to the data package

  Scenario: Verify access restrictions on private data package
    Given I have a private data package
    When a user outside my team tries to access the data package
    Then the user should be denied access
```

**(2) Step Definitions in Python:**

```python
from behave import given, when, then

@given('I am logged in as a Publisher')
def step_impl(context):
    context.publisher = login_as_publisher()

@when('I create a new data package')
def step_impl(context):
    context.data_package = create_data_package()

@when('I set the data package visibility to private')
def step_impl(context):
    context.data_package.set_visibility('private')

@then('the data package should be marked as private')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.data_package.visibility == 'private'

@then('only my team should have access to the data package')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.data_package.accessible_by(context.publisher.team)

@given('I have a private data package')
def step_impl(context):
    context.data_package = create_data_package()
    context.data_package.set_visibility('private')

@when('I share the data package with my team')
def step_impl(context):
    context.data_package.share_with(context.publisher.team)

@then('my team should receive access to the data package')
def step_impl(context):
    for member in context.publisher.team:
        assert context.data_package.accessible_by(member)

@then('no one outside my team should have access to the data package')
def step_impl(context):
    non_team_user = get_non_team_user()
    assert not context.data_package.accessible_by(non_team_user)

@when('a user outside my team tries to access the data package')
def step_impl(context):
    context.access_attempt = context.data_package.access_by(get_non_team_user())

@then('the user should be denied access')
def step_impl(context):
    assert context.access_attempt == 'denied'
```

**(3) Validation Checklist:**

- [ ] Verify that the Publisher can log in successfully.
- [ ] Verify that the Publisher can create a new data package.
- [ ] Verify that the Publisher can set the data package visibility to private.
- [ ] Verify that the data package is marked as private.
- [ ] Verify that only the Publisher's team has access to the private data package.
- [ ] Verify that the Publisher can share the private data package with their team.
- [ ] Verify that the team members receive access to the private data package.
- [ ] Verify that no one outside the Publisher's team has access to the private data package.
- [ ] Verify that a user outside the Publisher's team is denied access to the private data package.
